    {
      "id": "conditional",
      "name": "conditional",
      "category": "SelfAdjointView",
      "signature": "conditional(Target, Lower, Tri Mode, Triangular View)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "SelfAdjointView*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Lower",
          "type": "TriMode& ( Upper |",
          "default": "=(UpLo&(Upper|Lower))"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tri Mode",
          "type": "TriangularView<MatrixType,"
        },
        {
          "name": "Triangular View",
          "type": "TriangularView<MatrixType::AdjointReturnType,TriMode>>::type"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<unsigned int TriMode> EIGEN_DEVICE_FUNC",
      "docs": "\\returns an expression of a triangular view extracted from the current selfadjoint view of a given triangular part\nThe parameter \\a TriMode can have the following values: \\c #Upper, \\c #StrictlyUpper, \\c #UnitUpper,\n\\c #Lower, \\c #StrictlyLower, \\c #UnitLower.\nIf \\c TriMode references the same triangular part than \\c *this, then this method simply return a \\c TriangularView of the nested expression,\notherwise, the nested expression is first transposed, thus returning a \\c TriangularView<Transpose<MatrixType>> object.\n\\sa MatrixBase::triangularView(), class TriangularView"
    },
